# Dependencies
/node_modules/
/.pnp/
.pnp.*

# Build / test output (add your framework's dirs as needed)
/dist/
/build/
/coverage/
/out/

# Local env files — never commit real secrets.
# Broad on purpose: `.env` + `.env*.local` alone let `.env.production`,
# `.env.staging` and `.env.test` through, and this repository is public, so a
# file nobody thought to add here is published the moment it is created.
# `*.env` covers the other half of the habit (`production.env`, `local.env`).
#
# Still uncovered, on purpose: case variants (`.ENV`) and mid-name copies
# (`production.env.bak`). Both are matchable -- `[eE][nN][vV]`, `*.env.*` --
# and both were tried and dropped. `*.env.*` silently swallows an ordinary
# `docs/setup.env.md`, and a rule that hides files nobody asked it to hide is
# the same class of trap as a hook that silently does not run (Issue #75).
# Spelling every pattern three ways for the case variants makes the list
# unreadable, and an unreadable rule is one nobody maintains.
#
# So this list is the second line of defence, not the first. The one that
# actually holds is that credentials live in 1Password and in ADC, and never
# in a file in this tree at all.
.env*
*.env
!.env.example

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.pem
*.tsbuildinfo

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Sidecar local data dir (simplified-design-specification.md §23). The default
# is now the OS's per-user location, outside any checkout
# (`auto_scoring.api.sidecar.default_app_data_dir`, docs/windows-distribution.md
# §3), but `--app-data-dir ./app-data` is still a normal thing to type while
# developing, from any of the three directories tests and tools run in.
/app-data/
/backend/app-data/
/app/app-data/

# PyInstaller output for the bundled sidecar (`pnpm run package:sidecar`).
# The distributable artifact is built by CI, never committed.
/backend/build/
/backend/dist/

# Inno Setup output (`pnpm run package:installer`). The installer is a CI
# artifact, never committed.
/installer/output/

# Scratch state left by a Codex-based code-review run against this worktree
# (its CODEX_HOME and log, and any protocol-schema dump it generates while
# investigating a finding) -- tooling output, not project content.
/.review-codex-home/
/codex-review-*.log
/.tmp-review-protocol-schema/
